===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP}}

# On a [[level]] with the eye of the [[observer]], as of a picture hung in on a wall.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} At [[risk]], as in a [[contest]] or [[enterprise]].
#: {{ux|en|The survival of the company is '''on the line''' with this project.}}
#: {{rfdatek|en|Desperate Housewives}} I have a stalker. My life is '''on the line'''! - Gabrielle, from ''Desperate Housewives'' season 3 episode 13
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 26, 2019|author={{w|Kitty Empire}}|title=The Streets review – the agony and ecstasy of a great everyman|work=The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2019/jan/26/the-streets-mike-skinner-review-o2-academy-leeds
|passage= The 40-year-old is happy to put his body '''on the line''' in other ways, swapping a mug of tea for a fan’s double pint of lager and messily necking it in one. }}
# Currently calling on the [[telephone]].
#: ''I have John '''on the line''' for you.''
# {{lb|en|sports}} On one of the lines marked on a [[playing field]] or [[court]] and, hence, [[in bounds]].
#: ''The ball was '''on the line''' but the umpire ruled it out.''

